# Public history updates

The History page (`#history`) is a user-facing changelog in `app/history.ts`. Update it in the same change that warrants an entry. Newest entries first.

## Must add an entry

- **`kind: "rules"`** — any change to encoded permit logic, routes, quotas, eligibility, paperwork, or official sources in `app/permit-engine.ts` (or equivalent). Also when rules are re-checked against official sources, even if the outcome is “no change”.
- **`kind: "product"`** — a change a person using the wizard would notice and care about: new language, new covered route, new result they can act on, or a capability they can now use.

## Do not add an entry

Skip history for anything a user would not come to History to learn:

- dependency, security, or Dependabot updates
- typos, copy polish, CSS/layout tweaks, favicon/branding
- refactors, tests, lint, CI, gitignore, tooling, hosting/infra
- “we rewrote it as a static site” or other internal implementation moves

If unsure, skip. Wrong omission is better than a noise entry.

## How to write the entry

- Date: `YYYY-MM-DD` (use the effective/review date for rules, today for product).
- `title` and `body` in every current language (`Lang` in `app/permit-engine.ts`).
- Write for the user, not the repo. Say what changed for them, not which file changed.
- For official rule changes, set `source: { label, url }` to the primary public source.
- After a rules review, also refresh the “last reviewed” dates in `historyUi` and `ui.*.verified` / `ui.*.reviewed` in `app/permit-engine.ts`.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — user-relevant rules change
{ date: "2026-01-01", kind: "rules", source: { label: "admin.ch", url: "…" }, title: { en: "2026 work-permit quotas unchanged", /* de/fr/es */ }, body: { en: "On 19 November 2025 the Federal Council kept 2026 quotas at 2025 levels…", /* de/fr/es */ } }

// ❌ BAD — internal or minor
{ kind: "product", title: { en: "Fix npm audit vulnerabilities" } }
{ kind: "product", title: { en: "Clearer homepage and a matching mark" } }
```
